es allograft rejection and type of rejection in kidney transplant biopsy tissue; and AlloHeme, a monitoring test that predicts relapse in patients with acute myeloid leukemia and myelodysplastic syndromes. In addition, the company provides QTYPE that enables precision in human leukocyte antigen (HLA) typing; Olerup SSP, which is used to type HLA alleles based on sequence specific primer technology; and Ottr, a transplant patient management software. Further, it offers AlloSeq Tx, a high-resolution HLA typing solution; AlloSeq cfDNA, a surveillance solution to measure dd-cfDNA in blood; AlloSeq HCT, a solution for chimerism testing for stem cell transplant recipients; Allocell, a solution that monitors the pharmacokinetics of engraftment and persistence of cells for patients who have received allogeneic cell therapy; and XynQAPI, MedActionPlan, CareDx pharmacy, AlloHome, and HLA Data Systems software solutions. It has a license agreement with Illumina, Inc. for the distribution, development, and commercialization of NGS products and technologies. The company was formerly known as XDx, Inc. and changed its name to CareDx, Inc. in March 2014. The company was incorporated in 1998 and is headquartered in Brisbane, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John Walter Hanna Jr. | President, CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 761 people. Revenue per employee of $499K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 27%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $46K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["CareDx, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $4.1B market cap on $380M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +30% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -33% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 64% confirm genuine pricing power.","Shareholder yield of 2.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 8% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 856% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":8.558132866018799},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $7.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (CDNA)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/34/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_CDNA_112626070601_1795694761.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795694761.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CareDx (CDNA) May Find a Bottom Soon, Here's Why You Should Buy the Stock Now","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3034538/caredx-cdna-may-find-a-bottom-soon-here-s-why-you-should-buy-the-stock-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Chammer_chart_pattern_%28ta%29-3034538","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795528503.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CareDx (CDNA) Rallies as Medicare Coverage Decision Removes Key Reimbursement Headwind","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/caredx-cdna-rallies-medicare-coverage-161952614.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795191592.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.852,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Wall Street Analysts Think CareDx (CDNA) Could Surge 28.09%: Read This Before Placing a Bet","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3031131/wall-street-analysts-think-caredx-cdna-could-surge-28-09-read-this-before-placing-a-bet?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cconsensus_price_target-3031131","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794923703.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CareDx, Inc. (NASDAQ:CDNA) Stock Has Consensus Price Target of $70.33 According to Brokerages","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianon